  "rule": "Right-edge-anchored sockets have solid top and bottom rows and a solid right column, with a left-opening notch cut from the interior. A socket may have one loose same-colour piece further left: a full-height spine column with the notch shape attached on its right. The piece (leftmost object of its colour) is erased and translated by the unique translation that lands only on background and makes piece plus socket a solid rectangle. Its spine becomes a new column just left of the socket. Unpaired sockets and the background are unchanged.",
  "scope": "Random scenes: 8..20 rows and columns by default; explicit height 7..30 and width 8..30 are synthetic extensions. 2..4 right-anchored sockets in separate horizontal bands, heights 3..6 (3..7 when the grid is taller than 20) and widths 3..min(7 or 8, (W-2)//2). Random notches are often mirrored, about 25% are full-interior C shapes, and two-bay notches are possible. 1..k sockets are paired. Pieces are in disjoint row slots and usually start at column 0..3, further right on wide grids. Vertical offsets vary. Background defaults to 7 and is configurable. Explicit latent (sockets, pieces) arguments reconstruct the fixtures. Not supported: sockets on other edges, pieces right of their socket, same-colour decoys, multiple pieces per socket, pieces side by side in the same rows.",
  "constraints": [
    "Reviewed unique plug translation, unpaired distractor preservation and socket completion",
    "Bounds checks now precede notch allocation; malformed controls reject; random pieces cannot appear already inserted into foreign socket bounding boxes",
