  "authored_scope": "Random scenes: 8..20 rows and columns by default; explicit height 7..30 and width 8..30 are synthetic extensions. 2..4 right-anchored sockets in separate horizontal bands, heights 3..6 (3..7 when the grid is taller than 20) and widths 3..min(7 or 8, (W-2)//2). Random notches are often mirrored, about 25% are full-interior C shapes, and two-bay notches are possible. 1..k sockets are paired. Pieces are in disjoint row slots and usually start at column 0..3, further right on wide grids. Vertical offsets vary. Background defaults to 7 and is configurable. Explicit latent (sockets, pieces) arguments reconstruct the fixtures. Not supported: sockets on other edges, pieces right of their socket, same-colour decoys, multiple pieces per socket, pieces side by side in the same rows.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Socket colours are distinct and differ from the background.",
    "Each notch is non-empty, lies in interior rows 1..h-2 and columns 0..w-2, keeps the socket 4-connected, and every notch bay touches the socket's left column, so the piece is connected through its spine.",
    "Sockets are separated by at least one blank row.",
    "No piece cell lies in any socket's bounding box or in the column just left of it. This covers paired target rectangles and unpaired sockets' mouths.",
    "Pieces are not 8-adjacent to any other object.",
    "The piece starts strictly left of its socket's left column, so the leftmost-object rule identifies it.",
    "Exactly one non-zero translation of each piece lands only on background (or its own cells) and completes a solid rectangle with its socket, and it equals the constructed move.",
    "The background is strictly the most frequent colour.",
    "Explicit socket bounds are checked before any notch connectivity work. Malformed explicit structures raise ValueError.",
    "Rejection sampling is bounded at 500 attempts."
  ],
